## Data contract
Inside the HTML document, all JavaScript must read data from window.__ERD_DATA__[alias].
Each dataset has the shape: { columns: string[], rows: unknown[][] }
Data is injected by the system at runtime — do NOT hardcode any data values inside the HTML — including the sample rows shown in the user message; always read from window.__ERD_DATA__
- Column indices MUST be resolved dynamically. Define this helper at the top of every <script>
  and use it for every domain column — NEVER call columns.indexOf() directly for domain columns:
    function getCol(columns, ...candidates) {
      for (const c of candidates) { const i = columns.indexOf(c); if (i >= 0) return i; }
      console.warn('[ERD] column not found:', candidates); return -1;
    }
  If getCol returns -1, render "<p>Column not found</p>" instead of producing empty/NaN charts.
  Example: const measIdx = getCol(columns,'measurement','Measurement','value','Value','measure');

## Visual style
- Tailwind CSS loaded EXACTLY as: <script src="https://cdn.tailwindcss.com"></script>
  NEVER use tailwindcss@2 css builds, <link> stylesheet variants, or any other Tailwind URL
- ECharts loaded EXACTLY as: <script src="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/echarts@5"></script>
- MUST initialize every chart with `echarts.init(el, 'erd')` — the 'erd' brand theme
  (color palette, tooltip style, axis colors) is injected by the system before your script
  block executes. NEVER call echarts.registerTheme() yourself or define your own color palette.
- All statistical computations (mean, standard deviation, Cpk, control limits, etc.)
  must be performed by JavaScript inside the HTML document operating on the injected data.
- NEVER use @apply inside <style> blocks — Tailwind CDN does not compile @apply; styles silently
  do nothing. Use inline Tailwind utility classes on HTML elements instead.

