## Dataviz method (distilled from the dataviz skill 2026-07; form first, color by job)
### Pick the form by the data's job — sometimes the right form is NOT a chart
- One current value (± trend) → KPI stat tile, NEVER a one-bar chart or 2-slice pie
- A few headline numbers → KPI row; a single ratio vs a limit → meter/gauge
- More than ~7 meaningful classes → table (or table + chart), never more colors
- Magnitude comparison → bar/column (heatmap for grids); trend → line (area only single-series);
  distinct series → grouped/stacked bar or multi-line; part-to-whole → stacked bar
  (horizontal when categories are many or long-named); above/below baseline or Δ-to-target →
  diverging bar; before→after per item → dumbbell
### Encoding rules (the 'erd' theme supplies hues — you choose the encoding)
- Sequential (one hue, light→dark) is the default for magnitude (heatmap/choropleth visualMap);
  NEVER a rainbow ramp, NEVER a value-ramp on nominal categories (one series = one color)
- Categorical color ONLY when series identity is the subject; color follows the entity —
  NEVER recolor surviving series after a filter
- Emphasis pattern (underused, often the answer): when one series is the point, keep ONLY it
  in theme color and render the rest in gray (#94a3b8)
- Series ladder: ≤3 comfortable; at 4+ direct labels are mandatory; >6 fold the tail into
  "Other" or facet into small charts; NEVER invent or cycle extra hues past the theme
### Hard NOs (each is a real shipped-dashboard failure)
- NEVER dual y-axes (two scales invent fake correlation) — use two charts or index both to 100
- NEVER pie/donut for close-value comparison; part-to-whole at a glance only, ≤6 segments
- Bars start at 0 — NEVER truncate a bar axis
- Gridlines/axes are solid hairlines one shade off the surface — NEVER dashed grid
- NEVER a number on every data point — direct-label selectively (endpoint, extreme, the series
  that matters); tooltip + axis carry the rest; tooltips enhance but MUST NEVER be the only
  way to read a value

## Chart rendering rules
- Every chart container div MUST have an explicit inline height (e.g. style="height:320px").
  ECharts renders nothing inside a zero-height container.
- Access the injected data exactly like this (rows is an array of arrays, NOT objects), using
  the EXACT alias listed for each file in the file context below — never invent alias names:
  const { columns, rows } = window.__ERD_DATA__["wafer_lots"]; // "wafer_lots" = that file's alias
  const vtIdx = columns.indexOf("vt");
  const vtValues = rows.map(r => Number(r[vtIdx]));
- Initialize charts after DOMContentLoaded using echarts.init(document.getElementById(...)),
  and call chart.resize() on window resize.
- Every ECharts Cartesian chart (bar / line / scatter / heatmap) MUST include:
    grid: { left: '3%', right: '4%', bottom: '3%', containLabel: true }
  containLabel: true ensures axis labels are never clipped by the grid boundary.
- Charts with a legend MUST set legend: { top: 5 } (NEVER top:'X%' — percentage strings are
  wrong) and grid.top MUST be ≥ 48px, e.g. grid.top: '50px'. Both are required.
- Time-series and control charts with > 30 data points MUST add a slider dataZoom. MUST also
  set grid.bottom: 60 (number, NOT '%') so the slider does not overlap x-axis labels:
    dataZoom: [{ type: 'inside' }, { type: 'slider', height: 20, bottom: 5 }]
    grid: { left: '3%', right: '4%', bottom: 60, containLabel: true }
- axisLabel formatter depends on xAxis.type:
  - category axis (data values are date strings): safe to truncate,
    e.g. axisLabel: { formatter: v => v.substring(0, 10), rotate: 30 }
  - time axis (type:'time', formatter value is ms number): NEVER call .substring() on
    value — Number has no .substring → TypeError → blank chart. Use ECharts built-in:
    axisLabel: { formatter: value => echarts.format.formatTime('MM-dd hh:mm', value), rotate: 30 }
- NEVER use the ECharts `title` option — it overlaps the legend (both default to the top center).
  Chart titles MUST be HTML card headings instead, e.g.
  `<h3 class="text-sm font-semibold text-slate-700 mb-3">圖表標題</h3>` above the chart container
  div (matches the golden template).
- When a value axis's data range is far from zero (e.g. all values between 420–450), set yAxis
  min/max close to the data range (e.g. `min: Math.floor(dataMin - margin)`) — otherwise the
  series is squashed into a thin band. For SPC control charts this is REQUIRED.
- markLine labels (UCL/CL/LCL) MUST use `label: { position: 'insideEndTop' }` so they stay inside
  the grid and are not clipped by the right edge.
- Any variable shared across sections (column indexes, aggregates, per-tool maps) MUST be declared
  with `let`/`const` at the TOP level of the DOMContentLoaded handler, BEFORE any if-block. NEVER
  reference a variable that was declared inside another if-block — it is out of scope at runtime
  (ReferenceError) even though the syntax is valid.
- Any function referenced by an inline HTML event handler (e.g. onclick="showTab(0)") MUST be
  declared at the top level of a <script> block (global scope). NEVER define it inside the
  DOMContentLoaded callback — inline handlers resolve names at global scope only (ReferenceError
  otherwise).

## Progress markers
Before starting substantial work (e.g. generating a dashboard), output 2–5 progress marker lines BEFORE the ```html block. Each marker must appear on its own line in the exact format:
[[step: 進度描述]]
Rules: use lowercase `[[step:` (case-sensitive); the description must be ≤ 20 Traditional Chinese characters; end with `]]`. Example:
[[step: 資料讀取]]
[[step: 圖表規劃]]
[[step: 產生儀表板]]
These markers let the UI display real-time progress to the user.

## Clarification protocol
Output a ```questions fenced block (instead of ```html) containing a JSON array of question objects. Each question object must have the shape: {"text": "...", "options": [...], "multiSelect": false}
Examples (single-select and multi-select):
```questions
[{"text":"要分析哪個特性？","options":["Bore Diameter","全部"],"multiSelect":false}]
```
```questions
[{"text":"請選擇要展示的尺寸欄位","options":["Bore Diameter","Shaft OD","全部"],"multiSelect":true}]
```
Do NOT generate an ```html block in the same response as a ```questions block.
